From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Sep 2026 20:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: do not prepare a resume behind a pause on FEL

Preparing behind a pause seeks back for audio runway, which flushes video.
That closes the decoder's stream and cycles the frame providers, and the
Dolby Vision core drops its per-frame state when they go. It rebuilds that
state from the next picture it is given - but a preparation deliberately
withholds every picture until it releases, so on a stream decoding a full
enhancement layer the frame the video sink kept has nothing to composite it
and the whole output, overlays included, stays black until the pause ends.

Skip the preparation there. Those streams resume as they did before the
feature existed; everything else keeps it.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -4129,7 +4129,15 @@
          !m_pInputStream->IsRealtime() && !KODI::NETWORK::IsInternetStream(m_item) &&
          !m_pInputStream->GetIPosTime() && !m_pInputStream->GetITimes() &&
          !m_Edl.HasEdits() && !m_processInfo->GetVideoInterlaced() &&
-         m_State.time_offset == 0.0 && m_offset_pts == 0.0;
+         m_State.time_offset == 0.0 && m_offset_pts == 0.0 &&
+         // Preparing behind a pause flushes video, which closes the decoder's
+         // stream and cycles the frame providers. The Dolby Vision core drops
+         // its per-frame state on that and only rebuilds it from a new
+         // picture, so a preparation that then withholds every picture leaves
+         // the kept frame with nothing to composite it: the whole output,
+         // overlays included, stays black for as long as the pause lasts.
+         // Only a stream decoding a full enhancement layer carries that state.
+         !m_processInfo->GetDoviIsFEL();
 }
 
 bool CVideoPlayer::ResumeArmedPreroll()
